 "verdicts": {
  "q1": "inconclusive: one guarding signature (speed or concentration) beyond chance, not both",
  "q2": "no evidence of topic-specific tag-teaming: some pairs recur beyond the shuffle null, but the excess is no larger than on the comparison articles",
  "q3": "supports bloc voting: more high-agreement pairs and voting blocs than the stance permutation produces (consistent co-voting; on its own this is also what two honest camps produce, it is not proof of off-wiki coordination)",
  "q4": "inconclusive: fast reverters of critical-term removals overlap coord_edge_accounts, voting_bloc_members beyond matched random sets, but so do fast reverters of critical-term additions: a shared core of very active topic-area accounts, not removal-specific guarding",
  "q5": "primary source: 4 findings / remedies mention off-wiki coordination, canvassing, Discord, email or proxying (see arbcom.md)"
 }
